// Title: Enable BPF Kprobes Tracing
// Sigma ID: 7692f583-bd30-4008-8615-75dab3f08a99
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-01-25 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth
// Description: Detects common command used to enable bpf kprobes tracing
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://embracethered.com/blog/posts/2021/offensive-bpf-bpftrace/
//   - https://bpftrace.org/
//   - https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/v5.0/trace/kprobetrace.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_bpf_kprob_tracing_enabled.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "echo 1 >" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/sys/kernel/debug/tracing/events/kprobes/") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/myprobe/enable" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/myretprobe/enable")
